          ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above ${a}_{33}=-3$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}: &={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}: &={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}.$"
